  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q6",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "By first taking out a common factor, write each polynomial as a constant times a product of linear factors.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=3x^3+6x^2-39x+30$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3(x-2)(x-1)(x+5)$",
          "worked": "$$P(x)=3(x^3+2x^2-13x+10).$$\n\nLet $Q(x)=x^3+2x^2-13x+10$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(1)&=1+2-13+10\\\\Q(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nLong division by $x-1$ gives $x^2+3x-10$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=3(x-1)(x^2+3x-10)\\\\P(x)&=3(x-1)(x-2)(x+5)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=5x^3-5x^2-20x+20$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5(x-2)(x-1)(x+2)$",
          "worked": "$$P(x)=5(x^3-x^2-4x+4).$$\n\nLet $Q(x)=x^3-x^2-4x+4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(1)&=1-1-4+4\\\\Q(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nLong division by $x-1$ gives $x^2-4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=5(x-1)(x^2-4)\\\\P(x)&=5(x-1)(x-2)(x+2)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^4+x^3-4x^2-4x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(x-2)(x+1)(x+2)$",
          "worked": "$$P(x)=x(x^3+x^2-4x-4).$$\n\nLet $Q(x)=x^3+x^2-4x-4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(-1)&=-1+1+4-4\\\\Q(-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nLong division by $x+1$ gives $x^2-4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=x(x+1)(x^2-4)\\\\P(x)&=x(x+1)(x-2)(x+2)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe constant multiplier is 1.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^5+4x^4-2x^3-12x^2+9x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(x-1)^2(x+3)^2$\n\nTake out $x$, then use repeated zero testing and division.",
          "worked": "$$P(x)=x(x^4+4x^3-2x^2-12x+9).$$\n\nLet $Q(x)=x^4+4x^3-2x^2-12x+9$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(1)&=1+4-2-12+9\\\\Q(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nLong division by $x-1$ gives $R(x)=x^3+5x^2+3x-9$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}R(1)&=1+5+3-9\\\\R(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nLong division of $R(x)$ by $x-1$ gives $x^2+6x+9$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=x(x-1)^2(x^2+6x+9)\\\\P(x)&=x(x-1)^2(x+3)^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe constant multiplier is 1.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      }
    ]
